title: "Uniform lower bounds for Collatz predecessor densities: paper and Lean proofs"
authors:
  - family-names: Valbuena
    given-names: Lucas
repository-code: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction"
url: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction"
abstract: >-
  Natural Collatz basin densities satisfy a uniform inverse-linear lower bound
  at every positive target prime to three. Ordinary-map predecessor densities
  satisfy the same bound, and the canonical trace has a uniform positive lower
  bound at those targets. The proof combines Mazur's predecessor construction,
  Said Duran's coalescence theorem, and periodic source averaging. The paper
  also develops density and canonical-limit foundations from Tao's
  first-passage theorem and Mazur's natural-counting transport. The repository
  includes Lean sources, pinned dependencies, reproducible checks, and precise
  attribution. Divergence and additional cycles remain unresolved.
keywords:
  - Collatz conjecture
  - predecessor density
  - natural density
  - Lean
  - formal verification
  - canonical traces
